			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Beneath the bright face of the rebuilt {link:city-of-dalaran}City of Dalaran{/link} lies a city that its masters no longer fully command. The magi raised {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} anew behind their great barrier, and when the barrier fell, they opened their gates as if all were well. It is not. In places the restored city has slipped out of the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link}'s control. Spells turn upon their casters, constructs made to serve walk free, raw mana has taken shape and hunger, and something demonic has taken root where no demon should be. The Kirin Tor need help, and they are too proud to ask for it loudly.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[{link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} has been broken before. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} destroyed the city with a single spell, and the survivors spent years rebuilding it in secret. Such a work could not be done without vast outpourings of {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link}, wards laid upon wards, and servants bound by enchantment. How much of that old power still lingers in the stones, and how much of the demon lord's shadow, no one outside the order can say. The troubles within began before the barrier fell. Whether they caused its fall, no one has yet said.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Investigators of the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} speak of a disturbance that grows worse by the day, and of findings from a pylon they cannot yet explain. Their orders are to keep the city calm. Meanwhile the halls below have filled with things that should not be. Among them are a place called the {link:fel-grove}Fel Grove{/link}, where fel magic has seeped into living wood, and wandering shades of the dead.]=],
		},
